# No Comments Policy

Code should be self-documenting through clear variable names, function names, and proper code organization. Do not use comments in any file.

Key points:
- No inline comments (//)
- No block comments (/* */)
- No JSDoc comments
- No TODO comments
- No commented-out code

Instead:
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Break complex logic into well-named functions
- Use proper file and folder organization
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use TypeScript types for documentation

This applies to all files including:
- [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx)
- [src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/useMovies.ts](mdc:src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/useMovies.ts)
- [src/ui/components/Movies/Movies.tsx](mdc:src/ui/components/Movies/Movies.tsx)
